cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use canli-backtest, please cite the software and its author."
title: "canli-backtest: A backtester with fill-time causality and multiple-testing accounting"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Canli"
    given-names: "Arhan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arhancanli/canli-backtest"
url: "https://canlicapital.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - backtesting
  - look-ahead bias
  - overfitting
  - deflated Sharpe ratio
  - probability of backtest overfitting
  - walk-forward validation
abstract: >-
  canli-backtest is the simulation and validation layer of the ALPHAC research engine, published
  standalone. Decisions are separated from fills so a signal computed at a bar can only transact
  at a later executable price; execution realism covers borrow, financing, corporate actions and
  venue state; and a union trial ledger counts every hypothesis ever tested so deflated-Sharpe
  and probability-of-backtest-overfitting corrections use an honest denominator.
